sections.body:
Manager will, in Owner's name and for Owner's account:
- advertise vacancies and screen applicants with written criteria applied consistently and in compliance with fair housing laws;
- sign leases on Owner's approved terms, up to 12 months;
- collect rents, deposits and other charges, and handle late notices and, with Owner's approval, evictions through an attorney;
- arrange routine maintenance and repairs, and respond to emergencies 24 hours a day;
- conduct move-in and move-out inspections with photos, and handle deposit accounting within legal deadlines;
- keep complete records and comply with laws that apply to the Properties.

Owner will pay Manager:
- a management fee of {{mgmt_fee}}% of rents actually collected, with a minimum of {{min_fee}} per unit per month if stated;
- a leasing fee of {{leasing_fee}} for each new tenant;
- a renewal fee of {{renewal_fee}} for each renewal, if stated.

No other fees are charged unless Owner agrees in writing.
